    {
     "type": "note",
     "title": "Things are he, she or it",
     "md": "In English a thing is always *it*. In German the pronoun follows the **article** of the noun:\n\n- {de:der Kühlschrank} → **er**: {de:Er ist neu.}\n- {de:die Tasche} → **sie**: {de:Sie ist schön.}\n- {de:das Handy} → **es**: {de:Es ist alt.}\n- plural {de:die Stifte} → **sie**: {de:Sie sind praktisch.}\n\nSo a table is a „he“ (*der Tisch → er*), and a baby is an „it“ (*das Baby → es*). That's why you always learn a noun **with** its article."
    },
